  "configuration_id": "config_051",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_033 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) is the clear best at 0.725 acc, and all top-4 results share scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile. The only untested configuration in this top neighborhood is config_051 (same encoders, avgpool aggregation, concat fusion). It tests whether the aggregation/fusion interaction could yield a different local optimum when combined with the best encoders. While transformer+weighted (0.725) and transformer+concat (0.721) both outperform avgpool+weighted (0.706), avgpool+concat is the one missing cell in the 2×2 aggregation/fusion grid for the best encoders, and completing it reduces residual uncertainty. It is the highest-expected-accuracy option among all remaining untested configs (expected ~0.70–0.71, below the current best but well above alternatives using scgpt or pca). Expected cost is moderate (~4.5–5.0 GPU hours), comparable to config_042 (4.82) and config_017 (4.65), since it uses the same encoders and a lighter aggregation than transformer. As the final experiment, it is the best use of the last slot to either confirm the ceiling of the best encoder pair or (less likely) reveal a small surprise, while keeping total GPU hours in check."
}

